  "verbalization": "Arisugacin G appears to have a shared target, SNU-387, which is also the target of multiple related compounds, including 10,22-Dihydroxy-7,7,18,18-tetramethyl-8,13,17-trioxapentacyclo[12.8.0.03,12.04,9.016,21]docosa-1(22),3(12),4(9),10,14,16(21),19-heptaen-2-one and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. All these compounds are linked to SQ20B through a target relationship, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of a common molecular target. The evidence points to a possible role of SNU-387 in mediating the effects of Arisugacin G and its related compounds, potentially through a shared biochemical pathway or interaction. The consistent targeting of SNU-387 by multiple compounds supports the hypothesis that Arisugacin G may act through a mechanism that involves this target, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
